            <ArticleTitle>First adult patient with fibrosing colonopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1171-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An adult patient with cystic fibrosis and chronic abdominal complaints developed symptomatic fibrosing colonopathy several months after the beginning of high dose pancreas enzyme therapy. Despite the absence of a stricture, surgical resection was performed. Since then the abdominal complaints have not recurred.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
